<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="theory-extensions"
         xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
         version="5.0">

  <title>Theory Extensions</title>

  <para>
    A <emphasis>theory</emphasis> <mathphrase>T</mathphrase> over a signature
    <mathphrase>&#x03A3;</mathphrase> is a structure
    <mathphrase>T = (&#x03A3;, R)</mathphrase> extending
    <emphasis role="bold">LK</emphasis>, where <mathphrase>R</mathphrase> is a set of
    <emphasis role="bold">non-logical rules</emphasis>.
  </para>

  <section xml:id="non-logical-rules">
    <title>Non-Logical Rules</title>
    <para>
      Each non-logical rule <mathphrase>r &#x2208; R</mathphrase> has the form:
    </para>
    <informaltable frame="none">
      <tgroup cols="1">
        <colspec align="center"/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry rowsep="1"><mathphrase>&#x0393;&#x2081; &#x22A2; &#x0394;&#x2081; &#x2003; &#x22EF; &#x2003; &#x0393;&#x2092; &#x22A2; &#x0394;&#x2092;</mathphrase></entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><mathphrase>&#x0393; &#x22A2; &#x0394;</mathphrase></entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </informaltable>
    <para>
      where <mathphrase>n &#x2265; 0</mathphrase>. When <mathphrase>n = 0</mathphrase>,
      the rule is called an <emphasis role="bold">axiom sequent</emphasis> (a zero-premise rule).
    </para>
    <para>
      The following forms are permitted:
    </para>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem>
        <para>Multiple premises (<mathphrase>n &#x2265; 1</mathphrase>)</para>
      </listitem>
      <listitem>
        <para>Multiple antecedent formulas (multiset <mathphrase>&#x0393;</mathphrase>)</para>
      </listitem>
      <listitem>
        <para>Multiple succedent formulas (multiset <mathphrase>&#x0394;</mathphrase>)</para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
    <para>
      Theories may include the Cut rule explicitly in <mathphrase>R</mathphrase> or remain Cut-free.
    </para>
  </section>

</section>
